{{also|Grass}}
==English==
[[File:Steppe, Grassland, Rostov-on-Don, Russia.jpg|thumb|right|Grass.]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰreh₁-}}
{{dercat|en|gmw-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|gras}}, from {{inh|en|ang|græs}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*grasą||grass}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʰreh₁-||to grow}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|girs}}, {{m|sco|gers}}, {{m|sco|gress||grass}}, {{cog|frr|gäärs}}, {{m|frr|geers||grass}}, {{cog|stq|Gäärs||grass}}, {{cog|fy|gers||grass}}, {{cog|nds|Gras||grass}}, {{cog|nl|gras||grass, turf, pasture}}, {{cog|de|Gras||grass, weed}}, {{cog|da|græs||grass}}, {{cog|sv|gräs||grass}}, {{cog|nb|gress||grass}}, {{cog|fo|-}}, {{cog|is|-}} and {{cog|nn|gras||grass}}, {{cog|la|herba||plant, weed, grass}}, {{cog|sq|grath||grass blade, spike}}. Related to {{m|en|grow}}, {{m|en|green}}.
{{col-bottom}}

The "informer" sense is probably a shortening of {{m|en|grasshopper||police officer, informant}}, rhyming slang for {{m|en|copper||police officer}} or {{m|en|shopper||informant}}; the exact sequence of derivation is unclear.

