===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} Any [[plant]] of the [[family]] {{taxfmt|Poaceae|family}}, characterized by [[leaf|leaves]] that arise from [[node]]s in the [[stem]] and leaf bases that wrap around the stem, especially those grown as [[ground cover]] rather than for [[grain]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:grass}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|90|3|6|passage=Thou turnest man to destruction: and sayest, Returne yee children of men. / For a thousand yeeres in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past: and as a watch in the night. / Thou carriest them away as with a flood, they are as a sleepe: in the morning they are like '''grasse''' which groweth vp. / In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth vp: in the euening it is cut downe, and withereth.}}
#* {{RQ:Shelley Posthumous Poems|poem=Hymn of Pan|page=169|text=The cicale above in the lime, / And the lizards below in the '''grass''', / Were as silent as ever old Tmolus was, / Listening to my sweet pipings.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage='Twas early June, the new '''grass''' was flourishing everywheres, the posies in the yard—peonies and such—in full bloom, the sun was shining, and the water of the bay was blue, with light green streaks where the shoal showed.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Various plants not in family Poaceae that resemble grasses.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[lawn]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} [[marijuana|Marijuana]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:marijuana}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1970|author=Paul McCartney|title=Get Back|artist=The Beatles|album=Let It Be|passage=Jojo left his home in Tucson, Arizona / For some California '''grass'''}}
# {{senseid|en|informer}} {{lb|en|countable|Britain|slang}} An [[informer]], police informer; one who betrays a group (of criminals, etc) to the authorities.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:informant}}
#: {{ux|en|What just happened must remain secret. Don't be a '''grass'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Coding of a Concrete Animal|page=215|author=Paul Knight|year=2007|passage=He was a '''grass''' and an arse lick and he didn't do it for him, he did it for his brother, because if Vaughan had hit him especially with his mallet, Mark was the kind of lowlife that would have pressed charges and then that's a whole different problem.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=29 June 2023|journal=Metro|location=London|page=4|column=1|passage=Another claimed a &pound;10,000 bounty was put on his head as he was rumoured to be a “'''grass'''”.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|physics}} Sharp, closely spaced [[discontinuity|discontinuities]] in the [[trace]] of a [[cathode-ray tube]], produced by random [[interference]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} [[noise|Noise]] on an A-scope or similar type of [[radar]] display.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1960|publisher=United States. Bureau of Naval Personnel|title=Radarman 3 & 2|volume=1|page=49
|passage=The problem in radar detection is to have a signal to noise ratio that will allow the echo to be seen through the '''grass''' on the radar screen. The use of a long pulse allows a greater average signal strength to be returned in the target echoes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1963|title=Analysis of Weapons|page=61
|passage=Some of the scattered waves can be picked up by the receiver and may show up as "'''grass'''" on the radar presentation. Weather radars make use of this phenomenon to chart the progress of storms.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} The season of fresh grass; [[spring]] or [[summer]].
#: {{syn|en|breakup|spring|springtime}}
# {{lb|en|countable|obsolete|figurative}} That which is [[transitory]].
#: {{syn|en|ephemera}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Isaiah|40|7|passage=The grasse withereth, the flowre fadeth; because the spirit of the Lord bloweth vpon it: surely the people is '''grasse'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|folk etymology}} [[asparagus|Asparagus]]; "[[sparrowgrass]]".
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1769|author=w:Hannah Glasse
|title=[https://books.google.ca/books?id=L51gAAAAcAAJ&dq=the%20art%20of%20cookery%201765&pg=PR2#v=onepage&q=the%20art%20of%20cookery%201765&f=false [[Wikipedia:The Art of Cookery made Plain and Easy|The Art of Cookery made Plain and Easy]]]|edition=9th|page=195
|passage='Have ready a hundred of ſmall '''graſs''' boiled, then ſave tops enough to ſtick the rolls with, the reſt cut ſmall and put into the cream, fill the loaves with them.'}}
# {{lb|en|countable|mining}} The [[surface]] of a [[mine]].

